{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"msg_083d43b5d8a1ede5aa93aaec","type":"message","role":"assistant","model":"qwen3.6:35b-a3b-q4_K_M-agentic","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The issue is clear. The `median` function uses `ordered[len(ordered) // 2]` which returns the upper middle element for even-length lists. For `[1, 2, 3, 4]`, `len(ordered) // 2 = 2`, so it returns `ordered[2] = 3`. But the correct median for an even-length list is the average of the two middle elements: `(2 + 3) / 2 = 2.5`.\n\nFix: when the list has an even length, return the mean of the two middle elements.","signature":""}],"usage":{"input_tokens":27049,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"3a2f68dd-7bee-48e1-bb91-fc7612b87f40","uuid":"d90854ef-b4c2-46a8-99c0-79ef346071d6","timestamp":"2026-08-25T10:44:03.784Z"}
